From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 23:04:25 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 16/19] kcm: Say how large the screens are drawn

A Zoom label beside the View button gives the size of the screens in the arrangement view as
a percentage of their size in pixels, and follows Zoom In, Zoom Out, the wheel and Fit All.
wdisplays shows its zoom the same way.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5
---
 kcm/ui/main.qml | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kcm/ui/main.qml b/kcm/ui/main.qml
index 5ba9ebf0..e9555c38 100644
--- a/kcm/ui/main.qml
+++ b/kcm/ui/main.qml
@@ -489,6 +489,18 @@ KCM.AbstractKCM {
                 }
             }
 
+            QQC2.Label {
+                id: zoomPercentLabel
+                objectName: "zoomPercentLabel"
+                anchors.left: screenViewOptions.right
+                anchors.verticalCenter: screenViewOptions.verticalCenter
+                anchors.leftMargin: Kirigami.Units.smallSpacing
+                visible: screen.relativeFactor > 0
+                font: Kirigami.Theme.smallFont
+                // How large the screens are drawn: the pixels of the view for one pixel of a screen
+                text: i18nc("@info:status Size of the screens in the arrangement view as a percentage of their size in pixels", "Zoom %1%", Math.round(100 / screen.relativeFactor))
+            }
+
             QQC2.ToolButton {
                 id: screenEdit
                 anchors.right: parent.right
